UID:roze-filmdagen-2027-submissions@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Roze Filmdagen 2027: 30th Amsterdam LGBTQ+ Film Festival 
 Submissions
DESCRIPTION:The 30th Roze Filmdagen\, Amsterdam's LGBTQ+ film festival\, is
  accepting short films\, feature films\, documentaries and animations with
  a clear connection to LGBTQ+ themes and sexual\, gender and cultural dive
 rsity\, for its edition of 10-21 March 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Roze Filmdag
 en (Amsterdam LGBTQ+ Film Festival)\nLocation: Amsterdam\, Netherlands (30
 th edition\, 10-21 March 2027). Open to filmmakers worldwide.\nAward: Cash
  prizes (amounts not published): Jury Awards and Audience Awards for best 
 feature\, best documentary and best short\, plus the Free to be Me Award (
 initiated by Hivos). Roze Filmdagen is a nominating festival for the Iris 
 Prize (Cardiff). Listed under the desk's festival exception. Submission fe
 e: none in the 2025 and 2026 editions\; the 2027 FilmFreeway fee could not
  be confirmed.\nDuration: Festival 10-21 March 2027\n\nMore: https://rozef
 ilmdagen.nl/en/news/inzendingen-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://rozefilmdagen.nl/en/news/inzendingen-2027?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands (30th edition\, 10-21 March 2027). Open to
  filmmakers worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) runs this r
 esidency with Videotage\, a Hong Kong-based non-profit media arts institut
 ion specialising in the promotion\, presentation\, creation and preservati
 on of moving image and media art in all forms and languages.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL) in
  collaboration with Videotage\, Hong Kong\nLocation: Residency takes place
  at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must be established in the Netherla
 nds\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (K
 ingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within th
 e Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 for a two-month residency
  or EUR 6\,500 for a three-month residency\, paid by the Creative Industri
 es Fund NL to cover travel\, insurance\, living expenses\, compensation fo
 r time invested\, and material and transport costs. Accommodation\, use of
  the studio space and facilitation by Videotage are covered directly by th
 e Fund on top of this. No application fee.\nDuration: Two or three months 
 in 2027 (spring 2027)\; state your preferred period in the application.\n\
 nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must b
 e established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint
  Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in 
 a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:norma-fonds-projectbijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting NORMA: NORMA Fonds Project Grant (round 4\, 202
 6)
DESCRIPTION:The NORMA Fonds redistributes copyright remuneration collected 
 by Stichting NORMA into cultural\, social and professional projects involv
 ing performing artists\, and is one of the few Dutch schemes with four int
 akes a year and a genuinely short cycle.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting NORMA 
 (collecting society for performing artists)\nLocation: Netherlands-based a
 rts-sector activity. No city or region restriction stated.\nAward: Maximum
  EUR 10\,000 per project. Total project budget may not exceed EUR 150\,000
  and the applicant organisation's annual budget may not exceed EUR 500\,00
 0. At least 25 percent of the project budget must come from audience or bo
 x-office revenue. Performer fees must meet the 2026 wage norms of EUR 139 
 per rehearsal and EUR 340 per performance. No application fee.\nDuration: 
 Single project\, typically a production or concert series. Final report du
 e within six months of completion.\n\nMore: https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/
 norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restrict
 ion stated.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultuurloket-digitall-implementatiebijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cultuurloket DigitALL: Implementation Contribution (Imple
 mentatiebijdrage\, 2026)
DESCRIPTION:A one-off 2026 call letting Dutch cultural institutions reuse a
 nd adapt digital technology that other institutions have already built and
  published in the open DigitALL Toolkit\, for example translation software
  shared between theatres or a streaming platform adapted for a new venue. 
 Grants run up to EUR 30\,000 and cover technical modification\, integratio
 n\, production and deployment costs.\n\nOrganisation: Cultuurloket DigitAL
 L\nLocation: Netherlands and the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom. No city o
 r region restriction.\nAward: Up to EUR 30\,000. Covers technical modifica
 tion\, system integration\, production and deployment costs. Hardware purc
 hase alone is ineligible unless clearly essential to the public experience
 . No stated co-financing percentage. No application fee.\nDuration: Not sp
 ecified\; scoped to a single implementation.\n\nMore: https://cultuurloket
 digitall.nl/implementatiebijdrage/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://cultuurloketdigitall.nl/implementatiebijdrage/?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands and the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom. No city or reg
 ion restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-international-vouchers-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: International Vouchers
DESCRIPTION:Travel voucher for Dutch-based professionals in design\, archit
 ecture and/or digital culture who have been invited by a foreign party to 
 give a presentation\, lecture or workshop. To apply you must have submitte
 d an application to the Fund in the past five years that was positively as
 sessed (previous International Vouchers do not count).\n\nOrganisation: St
 imuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocatio
 n: Netherlands (for international travel)\nAward: Up to €1\,500 within E
 urope (zone 1) / up to €2\,500 outside Europe (zone 2)\nDuration: Per tr
 ip\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouch
 ers?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouchers?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (for international travel)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:filmfonds-netherlands-film-production-incentive-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherlands Film Production Incentive (October 2026 round
 )
DESCRIPTION:The Netherlands Film Production Incentive is the Film Fund's au
 tomatic cash rebate for feature films\, animated films and documentaries\,
  returning up to 35 percent of qualifying Dutch production costs. It is de
 signed to keep production spend in the Netherlands and is assessed on a po
 ints system rather than artistic panel review.\n\nOrganisation: Netherland
 s Film Fund (Nederlands Filmfonds)\nLocation: Netherlands. Applicant produ
 ction companies must be legally registered in the Netherlands\, including 
 Bonaire\, Sint Eustatius and Saba.\nAward: Cash rebate of up to 35 percent
  of qualifying Dutch production costs\, capped at EUR 3 million per year p
 er applicant production company. The annual budget is EUR 20 million divid
 ed across four rounds at roughly EUR 5 million per round\, with an extra E
 UR 3 million in the first round. No application fee.\nDuration: Per-projec
 t production incentive\, applied for per round\n\nMore: https://www.filmfo
 nds.nl/en/funding/fund/netherlands-film-production-incentive?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.filmfonds.nl/en/funding/fund/netherlands-film-production-in
 centive?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Applicant production companies must be legally regist
 ered in the Netherlands\, including Bonaire\, Sint Eustatius and Saba.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:filmfonds-production-incentive-high-end-series-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherlands Film Production Incentive: High-End Series (O
 ctober 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The High-End Series strand of the Netherlands Film Production I
 ncentive extends the Film Fund's 35 percent cash rebate to high-end drama\
 , documentary and animated television series\, returning up to 35 percent 
 of qualifying Dutch production costs.\n\nOrganisation: Netherlands Film Fu
 nd (Nederlands Filmfonds)\nLocation: Netherlands. Only applicants from the
  Netherlands\, Bonaire\, Sint Eustatius and Saba may apply.\nAward: Cash r
 ebate of up to 35 percent of qualifying Dutch production costs\, capped at
  EUR 3 million per project per year per applicant production company. The 
 2026 annual budget is EUR 9.5 million across three rounds\, plus an additi
 onal EUR 0.4 million in the first round carried over from 2025. No applica
 tion fee.\nDuration: Per-project production incentive\, applied for per ro
 und\n\nMore: https://www.filmfonds.nl/en/funding/fund/netherlands-film-pro
 duction-incentive-high-end-series?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://www.filmfonds.nl/en/funding/fund/netherlands-film-production-in
 centive-high-end-series?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Only applicants from the Netherlands\, Bonaire\, Sint
  Eustatius and Saba may apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-art-projects-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Art Projects
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Art Projects scheme contributes to the co
 sts of realising a contemporary art project. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, cura
 tors\, critics\, publicists\, partnerships and organisations.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Stroom Den Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicant
 s from outside The Hague (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes pl
 ace in The Hague or otherwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hagu
 e artists must be registered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).\nAward:
  Maximum EUR 10\,000 per project\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant per cal
 endar year. Requests above EUR 5\,000 require at least 30 percent co-finan
 cing of the total budget from third parties. Artist fees\, production and 
 communication costs are eligible\; Stroom endorses the kunstenaarshonorari
 um.nl fee guideline. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the gr
 ant remains valid for up to two years after the decision meeting\, with 80
  percent paid upfront and 20 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https://
 www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-projects?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-p
 rojects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicants from outside The Hague
  (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes place in The Hague or othe
 rwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hague artists must be regist
 ered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-art-program-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Art Program
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Art Program scheme contributes to the cos
 ts of an art programme: a series of activities (exhibitions\, presentation
 s\, lectures\, workshops\, etc.) with an artistic\, substantive\, thematic
  and/or formal connection that take place within a certain period. It also
  covers exchange activities with other countries and programmes for guest 
 studios and artist-in-residencies.\n\nOrganisation: Stroom Den Haag\nLocat
 ion: The Hague\, Netherlands. Aimed at non-profit organisations\, artist i
 nitiatives\, collectives and independent curators/organisers\; applicants 
 from outside The Hague apply with a CV\, provided the programme benefits T
 he Hague's art climate.\nAward: Maximum EUR 10\,000 per application\, up t
 o EUR 20\,000 per applicant per calendar year. Requests above EUR 5\,000 r
 equire at least 30 percent co-financing of the total budget from third par
 ties. Compliance with the kunstenaarshonorarium.nl artist fee guideline is
  part of the assessment. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; th
 e grant remains valid for up to two years after the decision meeting\, wit
 h 80 percent paid upfront and 20 percent on the final report\n\nMore: http
 s://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-program?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-p
 rogram?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Aimed at non-profit organisations\, artis
 t initiatives\, collectives and independent curators/organisers\; applican
 ts from outside The Hague apply with a CV\, provided the programme benefit
 s The Hague's art climate.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-research-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Research
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Research scheme contributes to the costs 
 of a research project or artist-in-residency that feeds the development of
  new work and benefits The Hague's art climate.\n\nOrganisation: Stroom De
 n Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to Hague artists registere
 d with Stroom and to curators\, mediators\, critics\, publicists and other
 s professionally active in the contemporary art world\; applicants from ou
 tside The Hague apply with a CV.\nAward: Maximum EUR 5\,000 per research p
 roject\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant per calendar year. Amounts exclud
 e VAT and grants are only awarded on demonstrable financial need. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the grant remains valid for up to t
 wo years after the decision meeting\, with 80 percent paid upfront and 20 
 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-a
 rtists/financial-support/pro-research?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-resea
 rch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to Hague artists registered with Str
 oom and to curators\, mediators\, critics\, publicists and others professi
 onally active in the contemporary art world\; applicants from outside The 
 Hague apply with a CV.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:go-short-nijmegen-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: Go Short 2027: International Short Film Festival Nijmegen
  Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Go Short\, the international short film festival in Nijmegen\, 
 is open for entries for its 19th edition (6 to 11 April 2027). A small\, a
 pproachable Dutch festival that programmes fiction\, documentary\, animati
 on and experimental shorts.\n\nOrganisation: Go Short\, International Shor
 t Film Festival Nijmegen\nLocation: Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Compe
 tition open to films made in Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Ar
 rivals Competition for European film school projects.\nAward: Small submis
 sion fees per tier: EUR 12.50 (early bird\, 15 September 2026)\, EUR 15 (r
 egular\, 15 November) or EUR 20 (late\, 15 December) for films\; EUR 8/10/
 12 for video games\, VR/XR\, performances and installations\; EUR 7.50 fla
 t for music videos. Awards include the Go Short Award for Best European Sh
 ort\, Best Dutch Short\, the New Arrivals Award and an Audience Award (amo
 unts not published in the call).\nDuration: Festival 6 to 11 April 2027\n\
 nMore: https://www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-202
 7?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goshort.nl/en/news-overview/call-for-entry-go-short-2027?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nijmegen\, Netherlands. European Competition open to films made in
  Europe\; dedicated Dutch Competition\; New Arrivals Competition for Europ
 ean film school projects.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-seed-grant-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T215458Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Seed Grant\, Autumn 2026 round
DESCRIPTION:The Stokroos Seed Grant supports early-practice visual artists\
 , designers and craft practitioners in the Netherlands with an unrestricte
 d budget for a self-defined plan: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\, EUR 7\,500 
 for duos\, EUR 10\,000 for collectives. The plan must start at least 10 we
 eks after submission\, last no longer than a year\, and can take place any
 where in the world.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLocation: Applica
 nts must live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Ca
 ribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; the funded plan itself 
